      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the two cases are mutually exclusive, determined by the sensor mode setting (sensor_mode):\n\n- Line ~443 (FP_MODE_FINGER_DOWN / standalone detection mode):\nThis handles the mode where the host explicitly requests a hardware interrupt when a finger touches the sensor without triggering image capture or processing immediately (e.g., waking up the host or dedicated finger detection requests). In this path, `send_mkbp_event(EC_MKBP_FP_FINGER_DOWN)` is sent directly, and execution skips heavy capture pipeline processing.\n\n- Line ~459 (FP_MODE_ANY_CAPTURE / Capture \u0026 Auth/Enroll mode):\nThis handles active image capture workflows (Enrollment, Matching/Auth, or Image Capture). In these modes, `FINGER_PRESENT` triggers image acquisition and algorithm processing (`fp_process_finger()`). The addition of `send_mkbp_event(EC_MKBP_FP_FINGER_DOWN)` here fires an immediate \"finger down\" event to lower HAL latency tracking before the heavier image acquisition/processing takes place.\n\nBecause `FP_MODE_FINGER_DOWN` and `FP_MODE_ANY_CAPTURE` represent different operational modes set in `global_context.sensor_mode`, a single IRQ evaluation cycle will not trigger both blocks simultaneously.\n\n\nThe one with Finger Down mode is tested in [test_finger_down_present](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/test/fingerprint/task/src/fpsensor_finger_presence.cc;l\u003d69?q\u003dplatform%2Fec%2Fzephyr%20EC_MKBP_FP_FINGER_DOWN\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch#:~:text\u003d68-,69,-70).\n\nI added a comment explaining the new event.",
